      <p class="muted">Source: cross-verified from cell-manufacturer datasheets and battery engineering references. Last verified: 2026-09-18.</p>
      <p class="muted">Return to <a href="https://worldbatteryhub.com">World Battery Hub</a>.</p>
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>Which chemistry has the longest cycle life?</h3>
<p>LFP generally offers the longest cycle life among common lithium chemistries, followed by LTO in high-power applications and NMC/NCA in energy-focused designs. The exact count depends on depth of discharge, temperature and end-of-life criterion.</p>
<h3>Why do the same chemistry values differ between sources?</h3>
<p>Cell design, electrode formulation, test temperature and the definition of end of life all change the result. The data site reports ranges and labels the evidence so that a single number is not mistaken for a universal specification.</p>
</div>
